"'''Silly Love Songs'''" is a song by the British rock band [[Paul McCartney and Wings|Wings]] that was written by [[Paul McCartney|Paul]] and [[Linda McCartney]]. The song first appeared in March 1976 on the album ''[[Wings at the Speed of Sound]],'' then it was released as a single backed with "[[Cook of the House]]" on 1 April in the US, and 30 April in the UK. The song, which features [[disco]] overtones, was seen as being written in response to [[music critic]]s accusing McCartney of predominantly writing "silly love songs" and "sentimental slush".

The song was McCartney's 27th American number one as a songwriter; the record for the most number one hits achieved there by a songwriter.{{refn|group=n|See the [[List of Billboard Hot 100 chart achievements and milestones]] for full clarification}} Despite its popularity, McCartney has not performed the song live since the dissolution of Wings.<ref name="Perasi" />

